{"id":"25742a41-e2ff-4880-bc9a-86ee7bacee66","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.neubiorev.2026.107083","title":"The World Federation of ADHD International Consensus Statement: 2026 Update","title_zh":"世界多动症联合会国际共识声明：2026年更新","doi":"10.1016/j.neubiorev.2026.107083","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neubiorev.2026.107083","abstract":"BACKGROUND: In the 5 years since the publication of the original ADHD International Consensus Statement, a great deal of new evidence has emerged. This updated consensus statement reflects the current state of the science with respect to ADHD, with a goal of reducing misconceptions and stigma around the disorder. METHODS: Studies eligible for inclusion were published between January 1, 2021 and July 1, 2025 and were either: 1) large cohort studies of 2000 or more participants, or 2) meta-analyses of at least 5 studies or 2000 participants in which publication bias was considered. Eligible studies were summarized and consolidated by theme. Manuscript contents were reviewed and approved by 118 authors from 29 countries and 6 continents. RESULTS: Two hundred and fifty-two empirically-supported statements were generated from these studies, offering readers an up-to-date understanding of the most robust findings in the areas of prevalence, how genes and environmental factors shape ADHD, psychiatric and somatic comorbidities, cognitive and neurological differences among individuals with ADHD, functional outcomes, and treatments for the disorder. CONCLUSIONS: Many of the conclusions of the original Consensus Statement are supported, but this update adds important nuance to some findings as a result of more recent evidence. It also highlights a few areas in which the balance of findings has shifted in the last 5 years, providing a transparent overview of the current scientific state of the field.","abstract_zh":"背景：自原版多动症国际共识声明发表以来的5年间，出现了大量新证据。本次更新版共识反映了当前关于多动症的科学现状，旨在减少围绕该疾病的误解与污名化。方法：纳入的研究需发表于2021年1月1日至2025年7月1日之间，且为以下两类之一：1）纳入2000名或更多参与者的大型队列研究；2）包含至少5项研究或2000名参与者、并考虑发表偏倚的Meta分析。合格研究按主题汇总整合。稿件内容经29个国家、6个大洲的118位作者审阅并批准。结果：基于这些研究生成了252条有实证支持的声明，为读者提供关于多动症最可靠发现的最新认识，涵盖患病率、基因与环境因素如何塑造多动症、精神和身体共病、多动症个体的认知与神经差异、功能结局及该疾病的治疗等领域。结论：原版共识声明的诸多结论得到支持，但本次更新根据更近期的证据为部分发现增添了重要细微差别。此外，它还凸显出过去5年中研究结论均衡发生转变的若干领域，提供了该领域当前科学现状的透明概述。","snippet":"BACKGROUND: In the 5 years since the publication of the original ADHD International Consensus Statement, a great deal of new evidence has emerged. This updated consensus statement reflects the current state of the science with respect to ADHD, with a goal of reducing misconceptions and stigma around the disorder. METHODS: Studies eligible for inclusion were published between January 1, 2021 and July 1, 2025 and were…","translated_at":"2026-11-19T00:01:45.422822Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"Review","volume":null,"issue":null,"published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-18T23:57:37Z","display_date":"2026-11-18T23:57:37Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Stephen V. Faraone","authors_text":"Stephen V. Faraone, Alison E. Pritchard, Mark A. Bellgrove, Jan K. Buitelaar, Li Yang, Luis Augusto Rohde, Brooke S.G. Molina, David Coghill, Jeffrey H. Newcorn, David W. Goodman, Tobias Banaschewski, Tanya E. Froehlich, Lenard A Adler, Haya F. Al-Joudi, Doron Almagor, Mohammed M.J. Alqahtani, Renato Arruda, Philip Asherson, Lukoye Atwoli, Paulo Verlaine B.e Azevedo, William J. Barbaresi, Ran Barzilay, Stephen P. Becker, Alessio Bellato, Sara Beomonte Zobel, Sven Bölte, Isabell Brikell, Ann C. Childress, Monica Conversano, Cleo L. Crunelle, David Daley, Søren Dalsgaard, Tycho J. Dekkers, Pietro De Rossi, Manfred Döpfner, Alysa E. Doyle, Stacey Espinet, Michael Fitzgerald, Barbara Franke, Martin Gignac, Jan Haavik, Holly K. Harris, Catharina A. Hartman, Cynthia M. Hartung, Stephen P. Hinshaw, Pieter J. Hoekstra, Chris Hollis, Nicole I. 